IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa17-helpers`

-- coa17-part21a-ch1.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 21A, Chapter 1 -- Introduction (ss 790A to 790CA;
-- lines 10177-10242 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. SOURCE, TARGET and HOW TO READ AN ANSWER are as
-- in coa17-part21-ch1.l4 (JUST TRUE: the text says yes; JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words; NOTHING: the text
-- does not decide; a caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE).
--
-- SEAMS (PLAN.md section 4). Schedule 1A (another part's) supplies the specified conditions and the rules on holding an
-- interest; the answers are INPUTS here, MAYBE BOOLEAN, named for the Schedule paragraph that answers:
--   `sch 1A para 1 the individual meets at least one of the specified conditions in relation to the company`  (s 790C(2), (3))
--   `sch 1A para 8 the person holds an interest in the company` and `sch 1A para 9 the interest is held through a legal entity` (s 790C(4), (8), (9)(a))
-- "body corporate" and "firm" come from the keel (s 1173(1)); a NOTHING input makes the answer NOTHING.
-- Section 790A (the overview) and subsections (1), (11), (13) and (14) of s 790C, and s 790B(2) and (4), are not rules for a
-- person (inert, reasons 1 and 2 in NOTES.md).

-- FORKS in this module (NOTES.md, "Fork register (coa17)", gives each reading and the text that licenses it; the
-- coverage table points each row at its fork): F4 at s 790B(1); F6 at s 790C(7); F13 at s 790C(4), s 790C(8).

§ `Part 21A Chapter 1: Introduction`

§§ `Companies to which this Part applies (s 790B)`

-- src:10186 | (1) This Part applies to companies other than—
-- src:10187 | (a) companies with voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market, and
-- src:10188 | (b) companies of any description specified by the Secretary of State by regulations.
@ref s 790B(1) Companies to which this Part applies (src:10186-10188)
GIVEN `the company has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has voting shares admitted to trading on an EU regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is of a description specified by the Secretary of State by regulations under section 790B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `the company has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` OR `the company has voting shares admitted to trading on an EU regulated market`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to companies other than— (a) companies with voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market" (fork F4)
    ELSE IF `the company is of a description specified by the Secretary of State by regulations under section 790B`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to companies other than— ... (b) companies of any description specified by the Secretary of State by regulations"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10192 | (5) In this section—
-- src:10193 | “voting shares” means shares carrying voting rights;
-- src:10194 | “voting rights” means rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question, including rights that arise only in certain circumstances.
@ref s 790B(5) "voting shares" and "voting rights" (src:10192-10194)
GIVEN `the shares carry voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790B(5) the shares are voting shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares carry voting rights`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voting shares” means shares carrying voting rights"

@ref s 790B(5) "voting rights" (src:10194)
GIVEN `the rights are rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question, including rights that arise only in certain circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790B(5) the rights are voting rights` MEANS
    IF `the rights are rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question, including rights that arise only in certain circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voting rights” means rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question"

§§ `Key terms (s 790C)`

-- src:10197 | (2) References to a person with (or having) “significant control” over a company are to an individual who meets one or more of the specified conditions in relation to the company.
-- src:10198 | (3) The “specified conditions” are those specified in Part 1 of Schedule 1A.
@ref s 790C(2) and (3) A person with "significant control"; the "specified conditions" (src:10197-10198)
GIVEN `the person is an individual, or is read as an individual by section 790C(12)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 1A para 1 the individual meets at least one of the specified conditions in relation to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(2) the person has significant control over the company` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is an individual, or is read as an individual by section 790C(12)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References to a person with (or having) “significant control” over a company are to an individual who meets one or more of the specified conditions"
    ELSE CONSIDER `sch 1A para 1 the individual meets at least one of the specified conditions in relation to the company`
         WHEN JUST x THEN
             IF x
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are to an individual who meets one or more of the specified conditions"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the specified conditions are those in Part 1 of Schedule 1A (s 790C(3)), which is another part's

-- src:10199 | (4) Individuals with significant control over a company are either “registrable” or “ non-registrable ” in relation to the company—
-- src:10200 | (a) they are “non-registrable” if they do not hold any interest in the company except through one or more legal entities over each of which they have significant control and—
-- src:10201 | (i) as respects any shares or right in the company which they hold indirectly as described in paragraph 9(1)(b)(i) of Schedule 1A, the legal entity through which the shares or right are held is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company; and
-- src:10202 | (ii) as respects any shares or right in the company which they hold indirectly as described in paragraph 9(1)(b)(ii) of Schedule 1A, at least one of the legal entities in the chain is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company
-- src:10203 | (b) otherwise, they are “registrable”,
-- src:10204 | and references to a “ registrable person ” in relation to a company are to an individual with significant control over the company who is registrable in relation to that company.
@ref s 790C(4) registrable and non-registrable individuals (src:10199-10204)
DECLARE `s 790C(4) way of holding indirectly` IS ONE OF
    `s 790C(4)(a)(i) as described in paragraph 9(1)(b)(i) of Schedule 1A`
    `s 790C(4)(a)(ii) as described in paragraph 9(1)(b)(ii) of Schedule 1A`

DECLARE `s 790C(4) holding through a legal entity` HAS
    `s 790C(4)(a) significant control over the legal entity (see s 790C(9)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 790C(4)(a) how the shares or right are held indirectly` IS A `s 790C(4) way of holding indirectly`
    `s 790C(4)(a)(i) the legal entity through which the shares or right are held is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 790C(4)(a)(ii) at least one of the legal entities in the chain is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

@ref s 790C(4)(a)(i) and (ii) the legal entities through which the shares or right are held (src:10200-10203)
GIVEN holding IS A `s 790C(4) holding through a legal entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(4)(a)(i) and (ii) a relevant legal entity is among the legal entities through which the shares or right are held` MEANS
    CONSIDER holding's `s 790C(4)(a) how the shares or right are held indirectly`
    WHEN `s 790C(4)(a)(i) as described in paragraph 9(1)(b)(i) of Schedule 1A` THEN holding's `s 790C(4)(a)(i) the legal entity through which the shares or right are held is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company`
    WHEN `s 790C(4)(a)(ii) as described in paragraph 9(1)(b)(ii) of Schedule 1A` THEN holding's `s 790C(4)(a)(ii) at least one of the legal entities in the chain is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company`

@ref s 790C(4)(a) each legal entity is one over which they have significant control, and (i) or (ii) holds (src:10200-10203)
GIVEN holding IS A `s 790C(4) holding through a legal entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(4)(a) the holding through a legal entity meets the conditions of non-registration` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        (holding's `s 790C(4)(a) significant control over the legal entity (see s 790C(9)(b))`)
        (`s 790C(4)(a)(i) and (ii) a relevant legal entity is among the legal entities through which the shares or right are held` holding)

@ref s 790C(4)(a) as respects any shares or right ... held indirectly (src:10200-10203)
GIVEN holdings IS A LIST OF `s 790C(4) holding through a legal entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(4)(a) every holding through a legal entity meets the conditions of non-registration` MEANS
    CONSIDER holdings
    WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN holding FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
            (`s 790C(4)(a) the holding through a legal entity meets the conditions of non-registration` holding)
            (`s 790C(4)(a) every holding through a legal entity meets the conditions of non-registration` rest)

@ref s 790C(4)(a) non-registrable (src:10199-10203)
GIVEN `the individual holds an interest in the company otherwise than through legal entities` IS A BOOLEAN
      holdings IS A LIST OF `s 790C(4) holding through a legal entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(4)(a) the individual with significant control is non-registrable` MEANS
    IF `the individual holds an interest in the company otherwise than through legal entities`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they are “non-registrable” if they do not hold any interest in the company except through one or more legal entities"
    ELSE CONSIDER holdings
         WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an individual with significant control who holds no interest of any kind is not dealt with by paragraph (a)
         OTHERWISE `s 790C(4)(a) every holding through a legal entity meets the conditions of non-registration` holdings

@ref s 790C(4)(b) otherwise, they are "registrable" (src:10203)
GIVEN `the individual holds an interest in the company otherwise than through legal entities` IS A BOOLEAN
      holdings IS A LIST OF `s 790C(4) holding through a legal entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(4)(b) the individual with significant control is registrable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 790C(4)(a) the individual with significant control is non-registrable` `the individual holds an interest in the company otherwise than through legal entities` holdings
    WHEN JUST nonRegistrable THEN JUST (NOT nonRegistrable) -- "(b) otherwise, they are “registrable”"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (a) holds is not decided

@ref s 790C(4) a "registrable person" (src:10204)
GIVEN `the person has significant control over the company (answer under section 790C(2))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the individual with significant control is registrable (answer under section 790C(4)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(4) the individual is a registrable person` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `the person has significant control over the company (answer under section 790C(2))` `the individual with significant control is registrable (answer under section 790C(4)(b))`

-- src:10205 | (5) A “legal entity” is a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed.
@ref s 790C(5) A "legal entity" (src:10205)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the person is a body corporate or a corporation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(5) the person is a legal entity` MEANS
    IF `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm`
    THEN IF `it is a legal person under the law by which it is governed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “legal entity” is a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the person is a body corporate or a corporation`
         WHEN JUST isBodyCorporate THEN
             IF isBodyCorporate AND `it is a legal person under the law by which it is governed`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “legal entity” is a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a body corporate is s 1173(1)'s answer, which is the keel's

-- src:10209 | (7) A legal entity is “subject to its own disclosure requirements” if—
-- src:10210 | (a) this Part applies to it (whether by virtue of section 790B or another enactment that extends the application of this Part),
-- src:10211 | (aa) it is an eligible Scottish partnership within the meaning of regulation 3(2) of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017.
-- src:10212 | (b) it has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market,
-- src:10213 | (c) it is of a description specified in regulations under section 790B (or that section as extended), or
-- src:10214 | (d) it is of a description specified by the Secretary of State by regulations made under this paragraph.
@ref s 790C(7) "subject to its own disclosure requirements" (src:10209-10214)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the legal entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is an eligible Scottish partnership within the meaning of regulation 3(2) of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is of a description specified in regulations under section 790B (or that section as extended)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is of a description specified by the Secretary of State by regulations made under section 790C(7)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(7) the legal entity is subject to its own disclosure requirements` MEANS
    IF    `it is an eligible Scottish partnership within the meaning of regulation 3(2) of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017`
       OR `it has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market`
       OR `it is of a description specified in regulations under section 790B (or that section as extended)`
       OR `it is of a description specified by the Secretary of State by regulations made under section 790C(7)(d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the legal entity`
         WHEN JUST appliesToIt THEN
             IF appliesToIt
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A legal entity is “subject to its own disclosure requirements” if— (a) this Part applies to it ..., (aa) ..., (b) ..., (c) ..., or (d) ..." (no paragraph holds; fork F6)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether this Part applies to the entity is section 790B(1)'s answer

-- src:10206 | (6) In relation to a company, a legal entity is a “relevant legal entity” if—
-- src:10207 | (a) it would have come within the definition of a person with significant control over the company if it had been an individual, and
-- src:10208 | (b) it is subject to its own disclosure requirements.
@ref s 790C(6) "relevant legal entity" (src:10206-10208)
GIVEN `sch 1A para 1 the legal entity would meet at least one of the specified conditions in relation to the company if it had been an individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the legal entity is subject to its own disclosure requirements (answer under section 790C(7))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(6) the legal entity is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `sch 1A para 1 the legal entity would meet at least one of the specified conditions in relation to the company if it had been an individual` `the legal entity is subject to its own disclosure requirements (answer under section 790C(7))`

-- src:10215 | (8) A relevant legal entity is either “registrable” or “ non-registrable ” in relation to a company—
-- src:10216 | (a) it is “non-registrable” if it does not hold any interest in the company except through one or more other legal entities over each of which it has significant control and—
-- src:10217 | (i) as respects any shares or right in the company which it holds indirectly as described in paragraph 9(1)(b)(i) of Schedule 1A, the legal entity through which the shares or right are held is also a relevant legal entity in relation to the company; and
-- src:10218 | (ii) as respects any shares or right in the company which it holds indirectly as described in paragraph 9(1)(b)(ii) of Schedule 1A, at least one of the legal entities in the chain is also a relevant legal entity in relation to the company;
-- src:10219 | (b) otherwise, it is “registrable”,
-- src:10220 | and references to a “ registrable relevant legal entity ” in relation to a company are to a relevant legal entity which is registrable in relation to that company.
@ref s 790C(8) registrable and non-registrable relevant legal entities (src:10215-10220)
GIVEN `the relevant legal entity holds an interest in the company otherwise than through other legal entities` IS A BOOLEAN
      holdings IS A LIST OF `s 790C(4) holding through a legal entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(8)(a) the relevant legal entity is non-registrable` MEANS
    IF `the relevant legal entity holds an interest in the company otherwise than through other legal entities`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is “non-registrable” if it does not hold any interest in the company except through one or more other legal entities"
    ELSE CONSIDER holdings
         WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a relevant legal entity that holds no interest of any kind is not dealt with by paragraph (a)
         OTHERWISE `s 790C(4)(a) every holding through a legal entity meets the conditions of non-registration` holdings -- the same test as (4)(a), with "also" a relevant legal entity

@ref s 790C(8)(b) otherwise, it is "registrable"; a "registrable relevant legal entity" (src:10219-10220)
GIVEN `the legal entity is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company (answer under section 790C(6))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant legal entity holds an interest in the company otherwise than through other legal entities` IS A BOOLEAN
      holdings IS A LIST OF `s 790C(4) holding through a legal entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(8)(b) the relevant legal entity is registrable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 790C(8)(a) the relevant legal entity is non-registrable` `the relevant legal entity holds an interest in the company otherwise than through other legal entities` holdings
    WHEN JUST nonRegistrable THEN
        `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `the legal entity is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company (answer under section 790C(6))` (JUST (NOT nonRegistrable)) -- "(b) otherwise, it is “registrable”"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `the legal entity is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company (answer under section 790C(6))` NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (a) holds is not decided

-- src:10221 | (9) For the purposes of subsections (4) and (8)—
-- src:10222 | (a) whether someone—
-- src:10223 | (i) holds an interest in a company, or
-- src:10224 | (ii) holds that interest through another legal entity,
-- src:10225 | is to be determined in accordance with Part 2 of Schedule 1A;
-- src:10226 | (b) whether someone has significant control over that other legal entity is to be determined in accordance with subsections (2) and (3) and Part 1 of Schedule 1A, reading references in those provisions to the company as references to that other entity.
@ref s 790C(9) how the questions in subsections (4) and (8) are determined (src:10221-10226)
DECLARE `s 790C(9) question for subsections (4) and (8)` IS ONE OF
    `s 790C(9)(a)(i) whether someone holds an interest in a company`
    `s 790C(9)(a)(ii) whether someone holds that interest through another legal entity`
    `s 790C(9)(b) whether someone has significant control over that other legal entity`

DECLARE `s 790C(9) where the question is determined` IS ONE OF
    `s 790C(9)(a) in accordance with Part 2 of Schedule 1A`
    `s 790C(9)(b) in accordance with subsections (2) and (3) and Part 1 of Schedule 1A, reading references to the company as references to that other entity`

GIVEN question IS A `s 790C(9) question for subsections (4) and (8)`
GIVETH A `s 790C(9) where the question is determined`
`s 790C(9) the question is determined` MEANS
    CONSIDER question
    WHEN `s 790C(9)(a)(i) whether someone holds an interest in a company` THEN `s 790C(9)(a) in accordance with Part 2 of Schedule 1A`
    WHEN `s 790C(9)(a)(ii) whether someone holds that interest through another legal entity` THEN `s 790C(9)(a) in accordance with Part 2 of Schedule 1A`
    WHEN `s 790C(9)(b) whether someone has significant control over that other legal entity` THEN `s 790C(9)(b) in accordance with subsections (2) and (3) and Part 1 of Schedule 1A, reading references to the company as references to that other entity`

-- src:10229 | (12) Subject to express provision in this Part and to any modification prescribed by regulations under this subsection, this Part is to be read and have effect as if each of the following were an individual, even if they are legal persons under the laws by which they are governed—
-- src:10230 | (a) a corporation sole,
-- src:10231 | (b) a government or government department of a country or territory or a part of a country or territory,
-- src:10232 | (c) an international organisation whose members include two or more countries or territories (or their governments),
-- src:10233 | (d) a local authority or local government body in the United Kingdom or elsewhere.
@ref s 790C(12) a corporation sole, a government, an international organisation or a local authority is read as an individual (src:10229-10233)
DECLARE `s 790C(12) kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 790C(12)(a) a corporation sole`
    `s 790C(12)(b) a government or government department of a country or territory or a part of a country or territory`
    `s 790C(12)(c) an international organisation whose members include two or more countries or territories (or their governments)`
    `s 790C(12)(d) a local authority or local government body in the United Kingdom or elsewhere`
    `s 790C(12) a legal person of some other kind`

GIVEN `the kind of person` IS A `s 790C(12) kind of person`
      `express provision in this Part or a modification prescribed by regulations under section 790C(12) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(12) this Part is read and has effect as if the person were an individual` MEANS
    IF `express provision in this Part or a modification prescribed by regulations under section 790C(12) applies`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to express provision in this Part and to any modification prescribed by regulations under this subsection"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the kind of person`
         WHEN `s 790C(12) a legal person of some other kind` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each of the following were an individual, even if they are legal persons under the laws by which they are governed— (a) ... (d)"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:10236 | (15) In this section “voting shares” has the same meaning as in section 790B.
@ref s 790C(15) "voting shares" has the same meaning as in section 790B (src:10236)
GIVEN `the shares carry voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(15) the shares are voting shares` MEANS
    `s 790B(5) the shares are voting shares` `the shares carry voting rights`

§§ `References to "confirmation" etc of information (s 790CA)`

-- src:10238 | For the purposes of this Part a company has had confirmation of—
-- src:10239 | (a) a person’s status as a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company,
-- src:10240 | (b) the required particulars of a person (see section 790K), or
-- src:10241 | (c) any other information about a person,
-- src:10242 | if the person has supplied that information to the company whether or not in pursuance of any duty imposed by this Part (and references to a company obtaining confirmation of information are to be read accordingly).
@ref s 790CA References to "confirmation" etc of information (src:10238-10242)
GIVEN `the person has supplied the information to the company, whether or not in pursuance of any duty imposed by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790CA the company has had confirmation of the information` MEANS
    IF `the person has supplied the information to the company, whether or not in pursuance of any duty imposed by this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company has had confirmation of— ... if the person has supplied that information to the company"
